x
x THE #1 SCRIPT-AUTHORING TRAP: a label's LAST line's commands are silently
x SKIPPED by the engine's label-fall-through. A label ending on a bare
x command (goto/battle/end/choice show/anything) never executes it - the
x story just falls through into the next label with no error. ALWAYS follow
x a label-ending command with a throwaway text line:  `...`\
x (it never displays when the command jumps or ends the cutscene). This bit
x two shipped games before it was documented - see CLAUDE.md gotcha #11.
